Presentation Structure

Each lesson presentation should follow the same structure to ensure consistency and maximize student engagement.

1. Title Slide

* Lesson number
* Lesson title
* Grammar/topic
* Learning objectives

2. Check-in (5–10 min)

* Greeting
* Icebreaker questions
* Personal conversation related to the lesson topic
* Review of previous homework (if applicable)

3. Warm-up / Lead-in (5–10 min)

* Picture discussion
* Brainstorming
* Prediction activity
* Short speaking task introducing today’s topic

4. Lesson Objectives

Students will:

* Learn…
* Practice…
* Be able to…

5. Vocabulary Introduction

* Target vocabulary
* Pronunciation
* Definitions
* Example sentences
* Visual support (pictures/icons)

6. Vocabulary Practice

* Matching
* Categorizing
* Fill in the blanks
* Speaking with new vocabulary
* Pair work

7. Grammar Presentation (when applicable)

* Clear explanation
* Form/structure
* Timeline (for tenses)
* Positive / Negative / Questions
* Signal words
* Common mistakes
* Examples

8. Controlled Practice

* Gap-fill exercises
* Sentence transformation
* Multiple choice
* Error correction
* Short written practice

9. Reading / Listening / Video (depending on lesson type)

Reading lessons:

* Pre-reading questions
* Reading text
* Vocabulary in context
* Comprehension questions
* Discussion

Listening lessons:

* Pre-listening prediction
* Listening task
* Comprehension questions
* Follow-up speaking

Video lessons:

* Pre-viewing discussion
* Video activity
* While-watching questions
* Post-video discussion

10. Speaking Practice

* Pair work
* Group discussion
* Role plays
* Information gap
* Debate questions
* Real-life situations

11. Production Task

Students use today’s language in a realistic communicative activity, such as:

* Conversation
* Storytelling
* Interview
* Presentation
* Debate
* Problem-solving task

12. Review

* Key vocabulary recap
* Grammar recap
* Quick quiz/game (Kahoot, Quizizz, etc.)
* Reflection questions

13. Homework

Include a balance of:

* Grammar practice
* Vocabulary revision
* Writing task
* Speaking preparation
* Optional challenge activity

14. Wrap-up

* Exit ticket (1–3 questions)
* “What did you learn today?”
* Self-assessment
* Preview of the next lesson

